From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arkadiusz Hiler <ahiler@codeweavers.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Jun 2025 18:36:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media-converter: Log tag file creation as error.

It's a first indicator to tell us that a game uses h264 or showed the
placeholder video. It would be nice to have this in the logs created by
proton without having to add the whole +dmo channel to list of the
default ones.

(cherry picked from commit 01866609e1e8d48595f75146821f3195b63c51c9)
---
 dlls/winegstreamer/media-converter/lib.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winegstreamer/media-converter/lib.c b/dlls/winegstreamer/media-converter/lib.c
index 39299b331ba..aef38d5846b 100644
--- a/dlls/winegstreamer/media-converter/lib.c
+++ b/dlls/winegstreamer/media-converter/lib.c
@@ -260,7 +260,7 @@ int create_placeholder_file(const char *file_name)
     char path[1024];
     int ret;
 
-    GST_INFO("Creating tag file %s.", file_name);
+    GST_ERROR("Creating tag file %s.", file_name);
 
     if ((shader_path = getenv("STEAM_COMPAT_TRANSCODED_MEDIA_PATH")))
     {
